ult=True\n2047 |         Set to False to perform inplace binarization and avoid a copy\n2048 |         (if the input is already a numpy array or a scipy.sparse CSR / CSC\n2049 |         matrix and if axis is 1).\n2050 | \n2051 |     Returns\n2052 |     -------\n2053 |     X_tr : {ndarray, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n2054 |         The transformed data.\n2055 | \n2056 |     See Also\n2057 |     --------\n2058 |     Binarizer : Performs binarization using the Transformer API\n2059 |         (e.g. as part of a preprocessing :class:`~sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`).\n2060 |     \"\"\"\n2061 |     X = check_array(X, accept_sparse=[\"csr\", \"csc\"], copy=copy)\n2062 |     if sparse.issparse(X):\n2063 |         if threshold < 0:\n2064 |             raise ValueError(\"Cannot binarize a sparse matrix with threshold < 0\")\n2065 |         cond = X.data > threshold\n2066 |         not_cond = np.logical_not(cond)\n2067 |         X.data[cond] = 1\n2068 |         X.data[not_cond] = 0\n2069 |         X.eliminate_zeros()\n2070 |     else:\n2071 |         cond = X > threshold\n2072 |         not_cond = np.logical_not(cond)\n2073 |         X[cond] = 1\n2074 |         X[not_cond] = 0\n2075 |     return X\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"sparse\", \"BSpline sparse\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `asv_benchmarks/benchmarks/datasets.py:_synth_regression_sparse_dataset`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n101 | def _synth_regression_sparse_dataset(\n102 |     n_samples=10000, n_features=10000, density=0.01, dtype=np.float32\n103 | ):\n104 |     X = sp.random(\n105 |         m=n_samples, n=n_features, density=density, format=\"csr\", random_state=0\n106 |     )\n107 |     X.data = np.random.RandomState(0).randn(X.getnnz())\n108 |     X = X.astype(dtype, copy=False)\n109 |     coefs = sp.random(m=n_features, n=1, density=0.5, random_state=0)\n110 |     coefs.data = np.random.RandomState(0).randn(coefs.getnnz())\n111 |     y = X.dot(coef